{"files":[{"content":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconstexpr int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    vector<vector<bool>> blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int y, x;\n        cin >> y >> x;\n        blockedCells[y][x] = true;\n    }\n\n    // dp[j] is the number of paths arriving from the preceding row.\n    // Once updated, dp[j - 1] is the current row's left neighbor.\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            if (blockedCells[i][j]) {\n                dp[j] = 0;\n            } else if (j != 0) {\n                int value = dp[j] + dp[j - 1];\n                if (value >= MOD)\n                    value -= MOD;\n                dp[j] = value;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"The horizontal recurrence is a true loop-carried dependency and should not be unsafely SIMD-vectorized; replacing the two-row implementation plus its full copy pass with a legal in-place rolling recurrence reduces per-row memory traffic while preserving exact modular results.","notes":"One bounded dependency-aware DP experiment. The in-place update reads the previous row at dp[j] before overwriting it and the current-row left value at dp[j-1].","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace two rolling rows and the post-row copy loop with one in-place rolling DP row.","Use one conditional subtraction for addition modulo MOD, since both operands are already reduced.","Enable buffered iostream input/output."]}